:false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-22T06:09:41Z","updated_at":"2025-12-06T10:42:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hello, I was looking through the metadata and wanted to clarify the labeling used in `emg2pose_metadata.csv`. \n\n1. The first column is named `session`, however in session `2022-04-07-1649318400-8125c-cv-emg-pose-train@2`, there is data that is not contiguous in time (there are other sessions that occur between stages of this session). The first continuous part of this session starts at `1649314883.5666700` and the second continuous part of this session starts at `1649398329.3833300`. \n\n2. It also seems like it is never defined what `demonstration` and `training` mean in the session label. \n\n3. This is just a small detail, but for some users, there seem like there are 2 sessions or 5 sessions, although the paper mentions users only have 3-4 sessions each. These 2 sessions seem to be the only sessions from another user: `2022-12-06-1670313600-e3096-cv-emg-pose-train@2`, `2022-12-06-1670313600-c3e72-cv-emg-pose-train@2`. These 5 sessions seem to be from one user: `2022-04-13-1649836800-a5d25-cv-emg-pose-train@2`, `2022-04-13-1649836800-45bfc-cv-emg-pose-train@2`, `2022-04-13-1649836800-8892f-cv-emg-pose-train@2`, `2022-04-13-1649836800-e6cfb-cv-emg-pose-demonstration@2`, `2022-04-13-1649836800-6e2c7-cv-emg-pose-demonstration@2`. ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/emg2pose/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebookresearch/emg2pose/is